# Code lines outside the chip-named trees that name a chip (sm####), for scripts/check.sh:
# "<path glob> :: <regex> :: <reason>", reason = "by design: ..." or an issue number. Shared code
# that names today's chips silently mishandles the next one, so this list only shrinks: fixing
# a leak deletes its row (a row nothing matches fails), and a new chip id without a row fails.
# Comments, devices/, kernel/, family docs and packages/soc/<name>-<soc>/ are not scanned.
config/pocknix.conf :: DEVICE:=sm8550 :: by design: the default image target
.github/* :: sm8550|sm8250 :: by design: the forms ask for the reporter's family
scripts/check-comments.py :: SM8550 quirk :: by design: self-test fixture
packages/shared/pocknix-bsp-common/pocknix-gpt-abl :: Retroid sm8250 units :: by design: help text naming the affected hardware
packages/shared/pocknix-openabl/* :: SM8250|SM8550|SM8750 :: by design: one OpenABL elf per supported chip, named by the release
packages/shared/pocknix-bsp-common/PKGBUILD :: linux-pocknix-sm[0-9]{4}<7 :: #126: the kernels that shipped the /flash deploy before it moved here
